<title>JAPAN: Japan August domestic vehicle sales fall 2.1 pct. [CORRECTED 09:05 GMT]</title>
<headline>Japan August domestic vehicle sales fall 2.1 pct. [CORRECTED 09:05 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle sales fell 2.1 percent in August from a year earlier to 290,144, the Japan Automobile Dealers' Association (JADA) said on Monday.</p>
<p>					  AUGUST  YR/YR PCT CHANGE</p>
<p>  Cars				  198,266	     +1.4</p>
<p>    - Over 2000 cc		   43,529	    -22.3</p>
<p>    - Under 2000 cc		 154,737	    +10.9</p>
<p>  Trucks				 90,747	     -8.6</p>
<p>    - Heavy			    12,009	    -30.4</p>
<p>    - Light			    78,738	     -4.0</p>
<p>  Buses				   1,131	    -31.5</p>
<p>  Total				 290,144	     -2.1</p>
<p>(Corrects categories for trucks to &quot;Heavy&quot; and &quot;Light&quot; from &quot;Over 2000 cc and &quot; Under 2000 cc&quot;).</p>
<p>Sales by the major manufacturers:</p>
<p>  Toyota		   106,121	     +0.1</p>
<p>  Nissan		    54,361	     -3.7</p>
<p>  Honda		     32,541	    +26.9</p>
<p>  Mitsubishi		27,660	    -13.8</p>
<p>  Mazda		     15,956	    -20.8</p>
<p>(Corrects figure for Nissan in table to 54,361 from 43,361).</p>
<p>Domestic sales of imported vehicles fell 2.9 percent from a year earlier to 26,544 in August.</p>
</text>
